From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: tegra: dfll: Allow the device tree to lower the maximum CPU frequency

The DFLL's maximum frequency comes from the SoC speedo table. Some
modules are validated for less: the Jetson Nano module's CPU is rated at
1479 MHz, while its speedo entry allows 1555.5 MHz.

Add an optional nvidia,dfll-max-freq-khz property that caps the maximum,
so the board's limit holds from boot without a userspace cpufreq policy.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/nvidia,tegra124-dfll.txt
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/nvidia,tegra124-dfll.txt
@@ -46,6 +46,10 @@
 Optional properties for the control loop parameters:
 - nvidia,cg-scale: Boolean value, see the field DFLL_PARAMS_CG_SCALE in the TRM.
 
+Optional properties for the frequency range:
+- nvidia,dfll-max-freq-khz: Highest CPU frequency in kHz. The DFLL does not
+  scale the CPU above it, even if the SoC's speedo supports more.
+
 Optional properties for mode selection:
 - nvidia,pwm-to-pmic: Use PWM to control regulator rather then I2C.
 
--- a/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-tegra124-dfll-fcpu.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-tegra124-dfll-fcpu.c
@@ -658,6 +658,7 @@
 {
 	int process_id, speedo_id, speedo_value, err;
 	struct tegra_dfll_soc_data *soc;
+	u32 max_freq_khz;
 	const struct dfll_fcpu_data *fcpu_data;
 	struct rail_alignment align;
 
@@ -695,6 +696,12 @@
 
 	soc->max_freq = fcpu_data->cpu_max_freq_table[speedo_id];
 
+	/* A board may limit the CPU below what its SoC supports */
+	if (!of_property_read_u32(pdev->dev.of_node, "nvidia,dfll-max-freq-khz",
+				  &max_freq_khz))
+		soc->max_freq = min_t(unsigned long, soc->max_freq,
+				      max_freq_khz * 1000UL);
+
 	soc->cvb = tegra_cvb_add_opp_table(soc->dev, fcpu_data->cpu_cvb_tables,
 					   fcpu_data->cpu_cvb_tables_size,
 					   &align, process_id, speedo_id,
